          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9.3.4 Image Formation by Lenses"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.275,
            0.114,
            0.899,
            0.15
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Lenses form images by refracting light. How do lenses form images? What is their nature? Let us study this for a convex lens first.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.312,
            0.171,
            0.484,
            0.193
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 9.12"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.3,
            0.208,
            0.874,
            0.239
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Take a convex lens. Find its approximate focal length in a way described in Activity 9.11.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.299,
            0.24,
            0.874,
            0.286
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Draw five parallel straight lines, using chalk, on a long Table such that the distance between the successive lines is equal to the focal length of the lens.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.3,
            0.287,
            0.874,
            0.317
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Place the lens on a lens stand. Place it on the central line such that the optical centre of the lens lies just over the line.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.3,
            0.317,
            0.875,
            0.365
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The two lines on either side of the lens correspond to F and 2F of the lens respectively. Mark them with appropriate letters such as",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 \\mathrm { F } _ { 1 } ,   \\mathrm { F } _ { 1 } ,   \\mathrm { F } _ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 \\mathrm { F } _ { 2 ^ { \\prime } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "respectively.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.3,
            0.364,
            0.874,
            0.395
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Place a burning candle, far beyond 2F "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "to the left. Obtain a clear sharp image on a screen on the opposite side of the lens.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.301,
            0.395,
            0.844,
            0.411
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Note down the nature, position and relative size of the image.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.3,
            0.411,
            0.875,
            0.457
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Repeat this Activity by placing object just behind "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 \\mathrm { F } _ { 1 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " between "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { F _ { 1 } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 \\mathrm { F } _ { 1 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " at "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { F _ { 1 } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " between "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{F}_{1}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "and O. Note down and tabulate your observations.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.276,
            0.483,
            0.899,
            0.517
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The nature, position and relative size of the image formed by convex lens for various positions of the object is summarised in Table 9.4.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.079,
            0.572,
            0.897,
            0.812
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_caption",
              "index": 12,
              "bbox": [
                0.073,
                0.532,
                0.898,
                0.568
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Table 9.4 Nature, position and relative size of the image formed by a convex lens for various positions of the object"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 13,
              "bbox": [
                0.079,
                0.572,
                0.897,
                0.812
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_18_table_13.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tr><td>Position of theobject</td><td>Position ofthe image</td><td>Relative size ofthe image</td><td>Nature ofthe image</td></tr><tr><td>At infinity</td><td>At focus<eq>\\mathrm { F } _ { 2 }</eq></td><td>Highly diminished,point-sized</td><td>Real and inverted</td></tr><tr><td>Beyond<eq>2 \\mathrm { F } _ { 1 }</eq></td><td>Between<eq>\\mathrm{F_2}</eq>and<eq>2 \\mathrm { F } _ { 2 }</eq></td><td>Diminished</td><td>Real and inverted</td></tr><tr><td>At 2F1</td><td>At<eq>2 \\mathrm { F } _ { 2 }</eq></td><td>Same size</td><td>Real and inverted</td></tr><tr><td>Between<eq>\\mathrm { F } _ { \\mathrm { 1 } }</eq>and<eq>2 \\mathrm { F } _ { 1 }</eq></td><td>Beyond<eq>2 \\mathrm { F } _ { 2 }</eq></td><td>Enlarged</td><td>Real and inverted</td></tr><tr><td>At focus<eq>\\mathrm { F } _ { \\mathrm { 1 } }</eq></td><td>At infinity</td><td rowspan=3 colspan=2>Image would not be formedVirtual and erect</td></tr><tr><td>Between focus<eq>\\mathrm { F _ { i } }</eq></td><td rowspan=2>On the same sideof the lens as theobject</td><td rowspan=2></td></tr><tr><td>andoptical centre O</td></tr></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.275,
            0.83,
            0.899,
            0.866
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us now do an Activity to study the nature, position and relative size of the image formed by a concave lens.",
